<title>JAPAN: Japan Sec cancels warning on NCB share lending.</title>
<headline>Japan Sec cancels warning on NCB share lending.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Securities Finance Co Ltd, which lends and borrows shares, said on Wednesday that it had cancelled its warning about possible problems in lending shares of Nippon Credit Bank Ltd (NCB).</p>
<p>Japan Securities did not elaborate on the move.</p>
<p>The company earlier this month issued a warning that there could be problems in lending the bank's shares to brokerages in the future.</p>
<p>Brokerages borrow stocks from Japan Securities for clients wishing to sell them short in margin transactions.</p>
</text>
